WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:35.507 --> 00:01:37.920
Bhopal is basically the capital

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:38.820
for Madhya Pradesh.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.670
Madhya Pradesh is the
central part of India.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:44.070
Majority we have middle class families

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.920
and many people migrating from villages.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.370
We have around 300 to 400 slum areas,

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.603
slum pockets also.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.990
In '92 me and my husband Anup

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:01.860
we started our organization
Aarambh in Bhopal.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.660
We started working with small projects.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.570
We started picking up children
near the railway stations.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.150
They were like basically the ragpickers.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:13.175
So we started a small
non-formal education center,

00:02:13.175 --> 00:02:15.516
taking out some money from our own pocket.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.780
We also run a number of projects

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.633
which have been funded by
different funding partners.

00:02:22.472 --> 00:02:25.440
One of the projects is the child help line

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.090
which is a government of India's project.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.000
And it has got a special number 1098,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.880
which is a pan-India number.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.340
And through Childline we ensure

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.010
that any child who has been exploited

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.923
or been abused, the child is protected.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:49.800
We have been working with
children, street children

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.140
and all kind of exploitation

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.640
which have been faced by children.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.820
But child marriage was
never a focus area for us

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:00.780
because we hardly got any call on this.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.580
Earlier people were not reporting.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.650
Now people are reporting.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.760
So now we come to know

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.127
that child marriage is
happening at a prominent level.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.870
And we start talking to them, discussing,

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.610
and then just making them aware

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:06.960
that you should not do this.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.030
So if people agree happily,

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:09.863
in that case,

00:04:09.863 --> 00:04:12.270
what we do is we take the entire family

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.230
to the police station

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.870
and then we have a document being prepared

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.040
in the police station

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.500
and that they will not
get their children married

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.090
before the age.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.470
In some cases

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:25.080
where the people become very adamant

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.580
they start fighting

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.775
then there's a whole community surrounded.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:29.010
Suddenly we had never realized

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:30.450
that 1098 will be flooded

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.490
with child marriage cases.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.530
Before Covid, 2017-18,

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:36.450
we had around 27 cases

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:37.740
and 2019-20

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:40.030
we had Covid, we had around 35

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:41.490
or 34 cases.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:42.930
And then 2020-21,

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:45.660
we suddenly, it was like 54 cases.

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:47.710
So it just shot up like that.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:50.063
There were many reasons.

00:07:50.063 --> 00:07:51.750
The government they're talking about this,

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:53.760
the marriage age should be increased

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.773
from 18 to 21 for a girl.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:59.430
So now most of the marriages are happening

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:01.080
because of that fear.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.220
There are a number of girls,

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.680
four or five girls in the family.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:06.840
Maybe now we have more families

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:09.780
who have lost the head of the family.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:10.770
And the mother is saying,

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.810
I won't be able to take care of them.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:15.870
They said we don't have
to invite many guests.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:19.113
In less expenses we can
get the marriage done.

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:32.550
Child marriage in India
is an issue in context

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:35.370
of the progressive laws of India

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:38.817
and the social context of India as such.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:44.850
With the tradition of
Indian society believing

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.530
in early marriages,

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:51.530
that heritage of belief
lingers on for centuries.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:55.800
And that's why after the
Indian constitution came up,

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.710
India introduced a lot of new

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:02.790
and progressive laws which
hit at the social norms.

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:05.610
And the whole issue of law enforcement

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:07.350
then becomes a challenge.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:10.325
The police forces is very concerned

00:09:10.325 --> 00:09:13.320
about creating an impact

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:17.640
by the exemplary effect
of enforcement of the law.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.500
You get information

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:20.700
and you suddenly go

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:21.870
and raid that place

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:22.800
and you do it.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.960
There is an exemplary effect.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.220
Other people come to know

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:27.423
that yes, this is wrong.

00:09:55.637 --> 00:09:59.160
For every five marriages prevented,

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.740
I would say there would have been 15

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:05.610
or 20 marriages not even taking place,

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:06.900
which would have taken place,

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:10.410
had these public education
programs would not

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:12.390
have taken place with the help of the NGOs

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:14.895
like Archana Sahay's NGO

00:10:14.895 --> 00:10:17.703
and other similar NGOs.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.540
I was born and brought up in Bhopal

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:09.330
and I studied in a convent school.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:11.850
Our sisters who used to teach us,

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:13.560
they used to do a lot of social work.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.150
They used to take us along

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.410
in the communities where they,

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:17.910
they did kind of,

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:20.070
some help to the families and all.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:21.690
So that all motivated me.

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:23.580
And I became gradually that,

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:27.180
helping people became a
part of my responsibility.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:39.872
Bhopal had faced the gas tragedy in 1984.

00:11:39.872 --> 00:11:42.513
At that time I was a
student of social work.

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:47.850
We got the opportunity to work
with these affected families,

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.980
especially with children

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.560
because many children were left alone,

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.150
their parents were dead.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.730
And then connecting them
with their extended family

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.313
that was one of the major
areas of what we did.

00:12:02.718 --> 00:12:04.680
And many children were also orphans

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:07.440
so we connected them
with the shelter homes,

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:10.020
we connected them with the orphanages.

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:12.600
Since then I wanted to work for my city.

00:14:22.203 --> 00:14:24.240
What we have done is the right thing

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:26.880
because it's not just about marriage,

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.260
it's about

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:29.760
what happens after marriage

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:32.100
if it is done before 18 years.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:35.010
There are health issues,
economical issues.

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:36.630
Maybe today she's not understanding,

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:38.220
tomorrow she will really understand

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:41.070
that what was done for her was right.

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:42.510
Now she's sad.

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:47.280
So this sadness is making us
feel a little uncomfortable

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:50.400
because she's already grown up

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:52.620
and we will be not in a position

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.630
to put her in a regular school.

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:55.983
So we feel bad.

00:14:57.780 --> 00:15:00.540
And we are not able to find out many ways,

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:02.220
many opportunities for her to

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:03.690
do something in her life

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:05.250
and do something for herself.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:07.650
Definitely this is a setback.

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:09.903
These issues teach us a lot.

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:21.240
When the child was being rescued

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:23.250
from the abusive situation.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:26.550
And now when I see the children doing good

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:29.820
and when the children call me back

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.220
and then they tell about their success,

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:33.960
their own family

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:36.000
and what they're doing,

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:37.710
and still they remember me

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:40.083
that's the most satisfying
thing which I get.

00:15:48.067 --> 00:15:49.140
To stand up,

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:53.100
to fight in this world of men,

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:57.780
to make my own position
was a big challenge for me.

00:15:57.780 --> 00:15:59.970
But I got support from my husband.

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:03.000
He said, I don't want you to be recognized

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:06.780
as my wife, I'll feel
proud when people will say

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:08.307
that I am your husband.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:13.740
There were quite a few
situations in all these 30 years

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.980
where people tried to put me down.

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:18.390
Because my father used to say

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:19.620
it's your fight,

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.210
you have to do it.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:22.560
So it was always my fight.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.226
And I'm happy

00:16:24.226 --> 00:16:25.238
that I have won.

00:16:25.238 --> 00:16:26.220
All the fights

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:27.053
I have won.

